<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's Bradesco, Salomon launch new fund.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Bradesco, Salomon launch new fund.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Private Brazilian bank Bradesco said it has launched an investment fund with U.S.-based Salomon Inc and its local associate Banco Patrimonio.</p>
<p>Bradesco said in a statement that the fund, Fundos Assets Manager, will have a diversified portfolio, including stocks and foreign and locally-issued bonds.</p>
<p>The fund, to be offered through Bradesco's 5,518 branches across Brazil, will seek investment from professionals, executives and businessmen, the statement said.</p>
<p>The banks also said the minimum required to invest in the fund is 20,000 reais ($19,378).</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415</p>
